    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d366">

                <pb facs="0334" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1869: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-08T13:00:00+03:25">May 8, 1942—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 8—12:19 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>145. Department’s 116, May 5 [<hi rendition="#italic">6</hi>].<anchor n="72"
                        xml:id="d366-f1"/> Prime Minister informed me last night he had received a
                    satisfactory reply from his appeal to Molotov reported in my 138, May 3. The
                    reply states that Soviet military authorities have been instructed to
                    collaborate with Iranian authorities with a view to sending Iranian troops to
                    disturbed areas.</p>
                <p>Minister of War<anchor n="73" xml:id="d366-f2"/> and several other officials have
                    already arrived in Azerbaijan to arrange the details with Soviet
                    authorities.</p>
                <p>A despatch on entire situation is being airmailed.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Kuibyshev.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d366-f1" n="72" xml:id="d366-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it informed the Minister in Iran concerning Department’s
                    instructions to the Ambassador in the Soviet Union contained in telegram No.
                    203, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d366-f2" n="73" xml:id="d366-f2-content">
                <p>Gen. Amanollah Jahanbani.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
